{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>By you shall Israel bless.</b> He speaks to Joseph, for by your seed shall the people of Israel bless, and they shall say to the one being blessed: 'May Elohim set you as Ephraim and as Manasseh.' <b>And he set Ephraim before Manasseh.</b> — That he preceded him to Manasseh in all his blessings, and even though he was the younger he did so because he saw his merit greater than that of the firstborn; and so the commentators explained." "<b>And it is fitting</b> to explain 'before Manasseh' as literally before him, and the intent is not the superiority of Ephraim in being prior to him, but rather the superiority of Manasseh the older brother; and it is like the expression (Genesis 44:14): ״ויפלו לפניו ארצה״. And Jacob's intention in this was to teach him discipline and proper conduct, and that he should show honor to Manasseh his older brother — like a person who places his fellow before one who is greater than him, because he is subordinate to him and follows his counsel. And since Ephraim the younger was destined to have advantage and superiority over the firstborn, the old man needed to place him now before Manasseh, to admonish him concerning his honor and that he should not grow arrogant over him on account of his great merit; as they said, of blessed memory: the extra ו״ו is to include your older brother."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:13.507344131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}